+          "quote": "Input a compact-box instance $(D_0,C,f)$ from [[def-spatial-global-optimization-problem]], a tolerance $\\varepsilon>0$, a positive integer node budget $N$, and a deterministic box-report oracle implementing [[def-spatial-box-bound-certificate]]. Every oracle call must finish in finite time or return an unavailable status. The budget counts each oracle call, including the root and both children after every split. The oracle may request higher precision on a repeated box; each such refinement is another counted call.\n\nInitialize a leaf ledger with the root box $D_0$, no incumbent, and zero calls. Before every oracle call, if the call counter is already $N$, return the complete current ledger with budget-exhausted; otherwise call the oracle and increment the counter by one. Store every returned field. A feasible witness $(x,U_x)$ updates the incumbent upper bound to $U=\\min U_x$. An empty-box proof marks that leaf empty. For constraints $g_i(x)\\le0$, a sound interval lower bound $\\underline g_i(B)>0$ is an empty-box proof. Store every valid lower bound $\\ell_B$ even if the leaf is later closed. A missing or non-finite required field returns inconclusive; it never becomes a bound.\n\nWhenever all current leaves have been evaluated, first return infeasible if they are all certified empty. Otherwise put $L=\\min\\{\\ell_B:B\\text{ is not certified empty}\\}$ if every nonempty leaf has a lower bound. If $U<+\\infty$, $L$ is finite, and $U-L\\le\\varepsilon$, return a feasible witness and the epsilon-global certificate $(L,U)$. Mark any leaf with $\\ell_B\\ge U-\\varepsilon$ closed while retaining its lower bound.\n\nIf no certificate is returned and no pending child awaits evaluation, split the nonclosed leaf with least lower bound; ties use creation order. In a box with positive widths, bisect a longest coordinate at its exact midpoint, using the least coordinate index among ties. The two closed children cover their parent. In the unconstrained mode, the oracle returns the exact midpoint as a feasible witness and exact objective value; the termination theorem uses this mode. For a zero-width singleton that has not been certified, request a deterministic higher-precision report for that same point; each refinement consumes one call. If refinement is unavailable, return inconclusive. When no certificate or infeasibility result has been established and another oracle call is needed after $N$ calls, the pre-call guard returns the complete current ledger with no optimality claim. This finite-budget procedure is global-search bookkeeping: a local stationary point or a solver tolerance is not a lower-bound certificate.",
